<title>USA: Marathon lowers most u.s. posted crude 25cts.</title>
<headline>Marathon lowers most u.s. posted crude 25cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil said it cut the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents a barrel, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $21.50 a barrel, West Texas Sour to $20.15 a barrel and Oklahoma Sweet to $21.50.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude remains unchanged at $19.50.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
